WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.122
The database contains a few small source areas.

00:00:03.122 --> 00:00:09.037
Patient and admission tables support healthcare-style views.

00:00:09.037 --> 00:00:14.427
Employee, department, and sales-order tables support a performance interface.

00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:18.077
Customer transactions support recent-activity and retention examples.

00:00:18.077 --> 00:00:26.592
Reusable objects are placed in an analytics schema so the source tables and analytical interfaces are clearly

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:33.702
separated. Connect this idea to a data platform materializing expensive summaries for faster consumption.

00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:39.742
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:47.692
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:47.692 --> 00:00:53.662
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:53.662 --> 00:00:59.562
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
